      "description": "<h2 data-section-id=\"15cf30v\" data-start=\"1099\" data-end=\"1136\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">Engelbert Humperdinck – Release Me<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchor\"></span></h2>\n<p data-start=\"1138\" data-end=\"1190\">Original Parrot Records stereo pressing (PAS 71012).</p>\n<p data-start=\"1192\" data-end=\"1318\">Classic late-1960s vocal pop album featuring Engelbert's breakthrough hit <strong data-start=\"1266\" data-end=\"1306\">\"Release Me (And Let Me Love Again)\"</strong> along with:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"1549\">\n<li data-section-id=\"w7q2fd\" data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"1332\">\nRelease Me\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"17b2e6z\" data-start=\"1333\" data-end=\"1347\">\nQuiet Nights\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1l7pz0h\" data-start=\"1348\" data-end=\"1370\">\nYours Until Tomorrow\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1b0bfis\" data-start=\"1371\" data-end=\"1395\">\nThere's A Kind Of Hush\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"ir3nth\" data-start=\"1396\" data-end=\"1413\">\nThis Is My Song\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1csfot4\" data-start=\"1414\" data-end=\"1427\">\nTen Guitars\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1kbvckt\" data-start=\"1428\" data-end=\"1454\">\nThere Goes My Everything\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"lb88j1\" data-start=\"1455\" data-end=\"1470\">\nTake My Heart\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1b33cq2\" data-start=\"1471\" data-end=\"1481\">\nIl Mondo\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"jq73oq\" data-start=\"1482\" data-end=\"1496\">\nTalking Love\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"bczai4\" data-start=\"1497\" data-end=\"1530\">\nWalk Through This World With Me\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1qan03u\" data-start=\"1531\" data-end=\"1549\">\nHow Near Is Love\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start=\"1551\" data-end=\"1554\">\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1uef3h1\" data-start=\"1556\" data-end=\"1569\">Condition</h3>\n<p data-start=\"1571\" data-end=\"1584\"><strong data-start=\"1571\" data-end=\"1584\">Vinyl: VG</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1586\" data-end=\"1763\">Record retains good shine with light scratches, sleeve scuffs, and hairlines consistent with normal use. No deep gouges observed. Expected to play with some light surface noise.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1765\" data-end=\"1778\"><strong data-start=\"1765\" data-end=\"1778\">Cover: G+</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1780\" data-end=\"1952\">Original jacket shows heavy shelf wear, staining, ring wear, writing on the front cover, edge wear, and age discoloration. Please review all photos carefully for condition.</p>",
